<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="824d6e15">&lt;p&gt;
    Test automation is a more efficient way to test by replacing manual efforts with automated ones. This type of
    testing better supports current testing trends such as Agile or continuous integration that require ongoing,
    iterative testing.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Test automation is used so tests are:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Repeatable&lt;/strong&gt; - as it performs the exact same steps during each execution
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Reusable&lt;/strong&gt; - since it can use the same test release after release in various environments
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Swift&lt;/strong&gt; - by leveraging automation tools that execute the tests faster than manual testing
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Test automation also allows for:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Increased application coverage&lt;/strong&gt; by executing faster allowing more time for the automated execution
        of additional modules
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Early defect detection&lt;/strong&gt; by validating new code drops more quickly
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Reduced time and costs&lt;/strong&gt; due to decreased manual efforts since automated tests can run
        unattended day and night
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Improved quality&lt;/strong&gt; of software
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Test automation can be used on various types of testing such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Unit / smoke tests
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Functional testing
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Structural testing
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Test data conditioning
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Installation and configuration
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Regression testing
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    EY has its own end-to-end Test Automation Framework, or eTAF, that focuses on the automation of functional and
    regression testing of applications. This framework is a library of components that is used to convert manual test cases
    to automated test scripts. The use of such a framework reduces maintenance thereby simplifying the automation
    effort even further.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The benefits of eTAF include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Centralized repository&lt;/strong&gt; - where all keywords, test cases, data, text execution and test results can
        be stored
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Easy setup and flexible framework&lt;/strong&gt; - that can be integrated with industry standard automation tools
        such as UDFT or Selenium
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        &lt;strong&gt;Built-in report and dashboard&lt;/strong&gt; - that presents users with a consolidated view of the latest test
        status and test execution results
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    For more details on eTAF, please refer to the &lt;a class=&quot;elementLink&quot;
    href=&quot;./../../../core.i_t.common.base/guidances/supportingmaterials/ey_auto_test_fmwk_handbook_C84252AD.html&quot;
    guid=&quot;_r4fEwES1EeiASMlqgAcI7A&quot;&gt;EY Automation Testing Framework Handbook&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
